# The backend quality gate. These live here rather than in a pyproject
# `[project]` table so they stay inside the machinery Phase A built: the
# compiled lock, --require-hashes, CI's drift check, and Dependabot's /backend
# pip entry. Pinned in a pyproject instead, the tools that police the build
# would be the one thing in it still floating.
#
# The ruff floor is not cosmetic. 0.16 is where the default rule set jumped from
# 59 rules to 413, so an unpinned ruff changes what "lint passes" means between
# two runs. pyproject.toml selects its rules explicitly, which makes the repo
# immune; this floor records that the immunity is deliberate.
ruff>=0.16.0
mypy>=2.3.0
